Prince of Persia 2: The Shadow and the Flame
Amiga port 0.90 (16.10.2026)

Release candidate under validation. Do not treat this file as evidence that
all release gates have passed. See docs/release.md in the source repository.

Requirements
------------
PAL AGA, 2 MB Chip RAM and at least 8 MB Fast RAM. The current validated timing
target is a 68030. 68020 support is deferred. 68040/MMU release validation is
in progress; hardware testing is planned on an A1200 68040/40 with 32 MB RAM.
WHDLoad and PRELOAD need memory in addition to the game's allocated memory.
Install WHDLoad and Installer 43 or newer separately. WHDLoad needs the A1200
Kickstart 3.1 image and its matching RTB in DEVS:Kickstarts, named
kick40068.A1200 and kick40068.A1200.RTB. Supply your own licensed ROM image.

Installation
------------
Supply your own unmodified Prince_Of_Persia2.SIT Macintosh archive:
SHA-256 02437dc253dffec4eee516f8e5e0f2ecaccc4bd31f3d6957d42ea4f87b80b080

The native Pop2InstallData helper extracts the archive and verifies its files.
Installation keeps the data uncompressed. No original game files, Kickstart,
Workbench or WHDLoad binary are included in the source or installer package.
Double-click Install and select the destination parent drawer and archive.
Allow 40 MB free, plus space to preserve an existing installation in .replaced.
The installer can reuse verified data and preserves saved games. Valid
preferences survive reinstallation; damaged preferences remain in the backup.
Double-click PrinceOfPersia2 in the installed drawer to launch with PRELOAD.
The WHDLoad launch workflow is still being validated.

Controls
--------
Space starts play. Use the original game's cursor keys and Shift controls.
Amiga-N: new game; Amiga-E: end game; Amiga-O/S: open/save; Amiga-Q: quit.
Amiga-P: pause; Amiga-T/M: sound/music; Amiga-R: restart; Amiga-H: hall of fame.
F10 exits WHDLoad. Saves are stored in the installation's Data drawer.

The game uses the original Macintosh instructions and game data. The Amiga port
provides display, sound, input and operating-system services. Ordinary builds
do not perform runtime SHA-256 scans, trap tracing or profiling.

